# The fixtures are real SQLite databases. Mark them binary so git never applies
# end-of-line conversion to them.
#
# Git's own heuristic would almost certainly get this right — these files are full of
# NUL bytes. Relying on the heuristic is the bug: the learner's workspace becomes a git
# repo they push, and on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true a file guessed
# wrong is silently corrupted. A corrupted fixture fails every test in the course with
# no hint as to why. (CONTRACT.md, Portability trap 1.)
* binary
